__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Generated by scripts/build_viquad_eval.py from taidng/UIT-ViQuAD2.0, whose
# license is not stated on Hugging Face -- not committed by default pending
# verification against the original UIT-ViQuAD paper/repo. See
# data/benchmark/PROVENANCE.md. (training_corpus_v1.json from
# build_training_corpus.py IS safe to commit -- CC-BY-SA 4.0 + MIT sources --
# and is not excluded here; commit it deliberately if you want it as the
# new default training corpus, together with an updated CHECKSUMS.json.)
data/benchmark/vcc_bench_uit_viquad_qa.json

# Trained model weights -- too large for git (GitHub hard-rejects blobs
# over 100MB, and models/slm/final/adapter_model.safetensors alone is
# ~300MB). Keep these out of version control; distribute via
# releases/artifact storage or Git LFS instead. NOT excluded:
# tone_probe.pt (a few hundred KB -- a small linear-probe classifier, not a
# full model) and the small adapter config/tokenizer files, which are safe
# and useful to commit alongside config.json/environment.json under results/
# so a run is traceable back to the model that produced it.
models/**/*.safetensors
models/**/*.bin
models/**/pytorch_model*.pt

# Canonical record stream and its splits (scripts/normalize_dataset.py ->
# scripts/split_dataset.py): ~470MB of text derived entirely from files that
# are already in git plus a recorded teacher run, so committing them would
# bury the repo for nothing. Rebuild with scripts/run_pipeline.py.
#
# The artifacts that make a run auditable ARE committed: split_manifest.json
# (policy, seed, realized ratios, eval document keys, output checksums),
# records_meta.json, verification_report.json, filter_report_*.json,
# CHECKSUMS.json -- and vcc_bench_eval.json, the independent eval set, which
# stays small and is what results are reported on.
#
# The two teacher-scale splits are NOT committed. vcc_bench_train.json passed
# 99MB once the teacher stage filled it, against GitHub's hard 100MB-per-file
# limit, and every regeneration would add another copy to history forever.
# Their sha256 in CHECKSUMS.json is what pins them.
data/processed/*.jsonl
data/processed/vcc_bench_train.json
data/processed/vcc_bench_eval_synthetic.json

# Teacher-LLM credentials (docs/dataset_pipeline.md §4). Never commit: the
# endpoint is billed per token and the key grants full access to it.
# Copy .env.example -> .env and fill it in; .env.example IS committed and must
# only ever contain placeholders.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Teacher-LLM stage (docs/dataset_pipeline.md §4/§12). Raw responses are kept
# on disk so re-filtering never needs a re-generation, but they are large,
# regenerable, and full of model output -- not repo content. The small
# reports (filter_report_*.json) ARE committed so a run stays auditable.
data/teacher/.cache/
data/teacher/*_raw.jsonl
data/teacher/*_raw.dryrun.jsonl
data/teacher/quarantine_*.jsonl
data/teacher/failures_*.jsonl
